=== Rivers and waterways ===

The principal river of Sant Cristòfor is the [[Riu Llobregat]], which flows from the Serralada d'Estret westward and then northward, forming part of the city's northern boundary before entering the bay near its northeastern corner. The Llobregat carries a significant sediment load, which has built a small delta at the bay's northeastern corner and contributes to the shallowing of the bay's northern shore. The river's lower reaches have been extensively channelised and canalised for flood control and navigation.

Several smaller streams (''riera'') drain from the Serralada foothills across the coastal plain into the bay, including the [[Riera de Sant Jordi]], the [[Riera de Sant Llorenç]], and the [[Riera del Mig]]. Most of these have been culverted or channelised through the urban area, though some retain open channels in the outer ciutats.

